# Program an IC Sorter: ores out of the middle port, and the first 10 loads of ice too.
# Everything else goes on out of the far end.
# d0: an IC Sorter.
# A filter is one number put into the sorter's memory. The low byte says what it tests:
#   SorterInstruction.FilterSortingClassCompare: class << 16 | comparison << 8 | 3
#   SorterInstruction.FilterPrefabHashEquals:    hash << 8 | 1
#   SorterInstruction.LimitNextExecutionByCount: count << 8 | 6  (the next filter only)
alias sorter d0
clr sorter
s sorter Mode 1    # Any: passing one filter is enough for the middle port
sll r0 SortingClass.Ores 16
or r0 r0 SorterInstruction.FilterSortingClassCompare   # comparison Equals is 0
put sorter 0 r0
move r0 10
sll r0 r0 8
or r0 r0 SorterInstruction.LimitNextExecutionByCount
put sorter 1 r0
move r0 HASH("Ice")
sll r0 r0 8
or r0 r0 SorterInstruction.FilterPrefabHashEquals
put sorter 2 r0
